From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:11:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/61] docs: ANOVA Certainty/robust, SD.cluster min_cluster,
 NNS.norm, meboot/MC rho

Roxygen and Rd, documentation only:
- NNS.ANOVA: Certainty is a descriptive similarity index, not a
  calibrated probability or the inverse of a p-value (same-distribution
  samples give medians of 0.73 at n = 30 and 0.96 at n = 1000, and the
  population adjustment shrinks small samples); robust draws independent
  bootstrap resamples (not permutations) and applies only to the
  two-sample path, not to pairwise / multi-group analysis.
- NNS.SD.cluster: describe what min_cluster actually controls (stop
  peeling once <= min_cluster variables remain; merge an undersized
  final cluster); peeled sets are not size-checked.
- NNS.norm: linear = FALSE is the dependence-weighted (nonlinear)
  scaling, TRUE the linear equal-means scaling (the text was inverted);
  note the positive-mean assumption and the 1e-10 zero-mean replacement.
- NNS.meboot / NNS.MC: rho targets the dependence of the detrended
  residuals (trend added back), so trending series stay correlated at
  rho = -1; NNS.MC lower_rho / upper_rho defaults are -1 / 1, not .01.
